From 18ae974bd4793d1b88d9600f137fab49e23ee470 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 17:08:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 29/41] drm/imagination: Add BXE-4-32 (36.50.54.182) as
 experimental

The BXE-4-32 MC1 found in the StarFive JH7110 is a single-cluster Rogue XE
core using a MIPS firmware processor. Imagination's device tables differ
from the already supported BXM-4-64 (36.52.104.182, TH1520) only in the
number of ISP IPP pipes (4 vs 6); the BRN/ERN set in the DDK hardware
definitions is identical, and the open-source firmware image
rogue_36.50.54.182_v1.fw carries matching device information.

Vulkan via Mesa's PowerVR driver (and OpenGL via Zink) has been exercised
on the VisionFive 2, but the core is not yet conformance tested, so list it
as experimental: loading the driver requires exp_hw_support=1, instead of
patching out the support check entirely.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015xcU1TUoi3P8rtmwjuUPqK
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/imagination/pvr_device.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/imagination/pvr_device.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/imagination/pvr_device.c
index 7de6bd360d..b66a01e17a 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/imagination/pvr_device.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/imagination/pvr_device.c
@@ -549,6 +549,9 @@ pvr_gpu_support_level(const struct pvr_gpu_id *gpu_id)
 	case PVR_PACKED_BVNC(36, 53, 104, 796):
 		return PVR_GPU_SUPPORTED;
 
+	case PVR_PACKED_BVNC(36, 50, 54, 182):
+		return PVR_GPU_EXPERIMENTAL;
+
 	default:
 		return PVR_GPU_UNKNOWN;
 	}
